---
// Glasserman & Lin (2023): backtesting GPT sentiment on headlines is biased when the model's training data
// overlaps the test period (look-ahead) and when general knowledge about a company colours the score
// (distraction). Their check compares original headlines with anonymised ones.
import DiagramIcon from './DiagramIcon.astro';
const W = 900;
const H = 400;
---
<figure class="p17g">
  <div class="p17g-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="A timeline with a line marking where a language model's training data ends. A backtest window before the line is risky because the model may already have read how those stocks moved. A backtest window after the line is clean. Below, two ways to feed a headline: the original, with the company name, and an anonymised copy where the company name is replaced by Company A.">
    <text x="20" y="28" class="p17g-h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>A language model has read the future of your backtest</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Mô hình ngôn ngữ đã đọc phần tương lai của backtest</tspan>
    </text>

    <line x1="40" y1="110" x2="860" y2="110" class="p17g-axis" />
    <rect x="60" y="70" width="330" height="24" rx="4" class="p17g-bt is-bad" />
    <text x="225" y="87" text-anchor="middle" class="p17g-btt">
      <tspan data-lang-en>backtest window A</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>cửa sổ backtest A</tspan>
    </text>
    <rect x="560" y="70" width="280" height="24" rx="4" class="p17g-bt is-ok" />
    <text x="700" y="87" text-anchor="middle" class="p17g-btt">
      <tspan data-lang-en>backtest window B</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>cửa sổ backtest B</tspan>
    </text>
    <line x1="470" y1="70" x2="470" y2="130" class="p17g-cut" />
    <DiagramIcon name="model" x="470" y="57" size="20" />
    <text x="486" y="62" class="p17g-s">
      <tspan data-lang-en>model's training data ends</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>dữ liệu huấn luyện của mô hình dừng ở đây</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="225" y="134" text-anchor="middle" class="p17g-bad">
      <tspan data-lang-en>may have seen how these stocks moved</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>có thể đã thấy các mã này diễn biến ra sao</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="700" y="134" text-anchor="middle" class="p17g-ok">
      <tspan data-lang-en>after the cutoff: clean</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>sau mốc cắt: sạch</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="20" y="170" width="420" height="160" rx="8" class="p17g-panel" />
    <text x="36" y="196" class="p17g-t">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Original headline</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Tiêu đề gốc</tspan>
    </text>
    <rect x="36" y="210" width="388" height="36" rx="6" class="p17g-card" />
    <text x="48" y="233" class="p17g-q">"Acme Bank posts record quarterly profit"</text>
    <text x="36" y="274" class="p17g-s">
      <tspan data-lang-en>The name lets the model recall what it knows</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Tên công ty cho phép mô hình nhớ lại điều nó biết</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="36" y="294" class="p17g-s">
      <tspan data-lang-en>about the company, maybe including the outcome.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>về công ty, có thể gồm cả kết cục.</tspan>
    </text>

    <polygon points="442,251 449,251 449,245 458,254 449,263 449,257 442,257" class="p17g-arrow" />

    <rect x="460" y="170" width="420" height="160" rx="8" class="p17g-panel is-ok" />
    <text x="476" y="196" class="p17g-t">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Anonymised copy</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Bản ẩn danh</tspan>
    </text>
    <rect x="476" y="210" width="388" height="36" rx="6" class="p17g-card" />
    <text x="488" y="233" class="p17g-q">"Company A posts record quarterly profit"</text>
    <text x="476" y="274" class="p17g-s">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Score both and compare. The gap measures how much</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Chấm cả hai rồi so sánh. Khoảng cách cho biết</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="476" y="294" class="p17g-s">
      <tspan data-lang-en>the model's memory of the company changes its answer.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>trí nhớ của mô hình về công ty làm đổi câu trả lời bao nhiêu.</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="20" y="372" class="p17g-note">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Window A is what most historical backtests use, because that is where the data is.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Cửa sổ A là thứ phần lớn backtest lịch sử dùng, vì dữ liệu nằm ở đó.</tspan>
    </text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Glasserman and Lin (2023) ran this comparison on GPT sentiment scores. "Acme Bank" is an invented name for the example.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Glasserman và Lin (2023) chạy phép so sánh này trên điểm cảm xúc của GPT. "Acme Bank" là tên tự đặt cho ví dụ.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .p17g { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .p17g-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .p17g svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .p17g text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .p17g .p17g-h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .p17g .p17g-t { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .p17g .p17g-q { font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--text); }
  .p17g .p17g-s { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .p17g .p17g-btt { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--text); }
  .p17g .p17g-bad { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--red); }
  .p17g .p17g-ok { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--gold-icon); }
  .p17g .p17g-note { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .p17g-axis { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .p17g-cut { stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .p17g-bt { stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .p17g-bt.is-bad { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); }
  .p17g-bt.is-ok { fill: var(--gold-tint-bg); stroke: var(--gold-icon); }
  .p17g-panel { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .p17g-panel.is-ok { stroke: var(--gold-icon); }
  .p17g-card { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.1; }
  .p17g-arrow { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .p17g figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
